    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">A <span class=\"learn-keyword\">drug</span> is any chemical substance that alters the functioning of the body or mind. Drugs used to prevent, treat or cure disease are called <span class=\"learn-keyword\">medicines</span>. Misuse of drugs is called <span class=\"learn-keyword\">drug abuse</span>.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Classification of Drugs</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Function</th><th>Examples</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Analgesics</td><td>Relieve pain</td><td>Aspirin, paracetamol, ibuprofen, codeine</td></tr><tr><td>Antibiotics</td><td>Kill or stop bacteria</td><td>Penicillin, amoxicillin, streptomycin</td></tr><tr><td>Antimalarials</td><td>Treat malaria</td><td>Chloroquine, quinine, artemisinin-based combination therapy (ACT)</td></tr><tr><td>Antacids</td><td>Neutralise excess stomach acid</td><td>Magnesium hydroxide (milk of magnesia), aluminium hydroxide, sodium hydrogencarbonate</td></tr><tr><td>Antiseptics and disinfectants</td><td>Kill germs on skin (antiseptic) or on objects (disinfectant)</td><td>Dettol, iodine, hydrogen peroxide</td></tr><tr><td>Stimulants</td><td>Increase alertness and activity</td><td>Caffeine, nicotine, amphetamines, cocaine</td></tr><tr><td>Depressants (sedatives)</td><td>Slow the nervous system</td><td>Alcohol, barbiturates, diazepam</td></tr><tr><td>Narcotics</td><td>Relieve severe pain; highly addictive</td><td>Morphine, heroin, codeine</td></tr><tr><td>Hallucinogens</td><td>Distort perception</td><td>LSD, cannabis (marijuana)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Medicinal Uses</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Aspirin is also an anti-inflammatory and reduces fever.</li><li>Antibiotics do not work against viruses.</li><li>Vaccines stimulate immunity; anaesthetics remove sensation during surgery.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Harmful Chemicals and Drug Abuse</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Drug abuse is the use of drugs for non-medical reasons or in excess. Effects include addiction (dependence), damage to the liver, kidneys, heart and brain, mental disorders, aggression, poor school and work performance, crime, and death from overdose. Sharing needles spreads HIV and hepatitis.</p><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Substance</th><th>Harmful effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nicotine (tobacco)</td><td>Addiction, lung cancer, heart disease</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>Liver cirrhosis, impaired judgement, accidents</td></tr><tr><td>Cocaine, heroin</td><td>Severe addiction, overdose, mental damage</td></tr><tr><td>Cannabis</td><td>Hallucination, mental illness, memory loss</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Control</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">In Nigeria the <strong>National Drug Law Enforcement Agency (NDLEA)</strong> fights illicit drugs and NAFDAC regulates drugs and food. Drugs should be taken only as prescribed and never shared.</p><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Summary:</strong> Drugs can heal or harm; the dose, purpose and supervision decide which.</div>",
